warning[NK1308]: `loose` reaches the path `fs::exists` opens under `fs::Root::Anywhere`, which may name any file, and it comes from outside the program.
   --> tests/a_guarded_join_carries_its_proof_to_a_binding.nika:18:5
    |
 18 |     println(fs::exists(loose, fs::Root::Anywhere))
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `loose` comes from `cli::args`: whoever sends it chooses the value, so nothing the compiler can see says what it holds.
    = note: A path from outside may name any file the program can reach: `../`, or one that starts at `/`.
    = note: `raw-sinks = "warn"` lets this build through.
    = help: Open it under a root the program chose, where it cannot leave the directory: `fs::Root::Dir(".")`, `fs::scratch()` or `root.join(...)` of one. Or check it where it arrives, `throw BadInput(loose) if !path::is_component(loose)` (or `path::is_below`), and open it under such a root or joined to a part that is not outside. If the program means to read paths from `args`, `untrusted-paths-read = ["args"]` under `[allow]` in the manifest builds it.
